# The design basis — this project's vocabulary, registry and invariants —
# together with the record of its hashes. A harness may propose a change
# to these on a branch; only xormania lands one.
#
# GitHub uses this to request review automatically and to label the
# ownership. It is enforcement only if branch protection requires code
# owner review, and on a solo repository that setting deadlocks: GitHub
# will not accept the author's own approval, so a pull request xormania
# opened could never satisfy it. The workable pairing is branch
# protection that requires a pull request into master with admin merge —
# which is how this repository already works — plus dev/lock, whose
# failure is what makes an unconsented change loud in the first place.

/dev/lexicon-workshop.cue  @xormania
/dev/lexicon-product.cue   @xormania
/dev/registry.cue          @xormania
/dev/tier0.cue             @xormania
/dev/LOCKED                @xormania
/dev/lock                  @xormania
